WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.130
Dusk.

2
00:00:01.180 --> 00:00:05.440
A dark plain, filled with
rows of tents and banners.

3
00:00:05.490 --> 00:00:07.490
A drum taps out a beat.

4
00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:11.680
"The Assyrian came down like the
wolf on the fold," By morning,

5
00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:14.800
the lights are out,
and the camp is silent.

6
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:17.090
No battle was ever fought.

7
00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:20.190
So why would Byron make this poem gallop?

8
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:23.660
In this mission, you'll uncover
the Bible story behind it:

9
00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:27.910
King Sennacherib's army
at Jerusalem, in 701 BC.

10
00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:30.660
You'll tap out the beat:
four gallops a line,

11
00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:32.940
called anapaestic tetrameter.

12
00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:36.980
And you'll look again at that
wolf, coming down on the fold.

13
00:00:37.030 --> 00:00:41.080
Your mission: explain why
Byron makes the poem gallop.
